  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "You'd think inherited money would last for generations. The uncomfortable data says most of it vanishes within a few years.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "home",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "x"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Inheritances",
            "vanish fast."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A large share of heirs spend or lose the bulk of what they receive surprisingly quickly.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "a few yrs",
          "label": "and much of it is gone",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Inheritance is the transfer of assets after someone dies.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-inheritance",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · inheritance"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The reason is simple and human. A windfall feels like free money, so it gets treated like free money.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "home",
          "kicker": "why",
          "line": "It feels free",
          "sub": "so it's spent like it"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Lifestyle jumps, big purchases, and no plan quietly drain it.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "No plan, no pile",
          "props": [
            "x",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Even the tax rules favor simply holding inherited assets, not spending them.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-steppedup",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · stepped-up basis"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And this matters now more than ever, with about eighty-four trillion dollars set to change hands.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "$84T",
          "label": "the great wealth transfer",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "globe"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Careful gifting while alive is one way families try to make it last.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-gifttax",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · gift tax"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Without a plan, a windfall just quietly funds a nicer version of the same old life.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "No plan, no pile",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And the tax system actually rewards holding it, not spending it.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-estatetax",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · estate tax"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s10"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So be honest, would your inheritance actually last?",
